&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To avoid the worst effects of climate change, most climate models agree the world will need to dramatically reduce emissions &lt;strong&gt;and&lt;/strong&gt; remove 5-10 billion tons of carbon dioxide from the atmosphere per year by 2050. The Climate team’s goal is to accelerate Stripe’s path to net zero in parallel with the world’s. We do this by reducing Stripe’s emissions and leading initiatives to increase the likelihood we build sufficient carbon removal capacity to reach global climate goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In 2019, we developed the first measurement of Stripe’s emissions. In 2021 we launched&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/climate&quot;&gt; Stripe Climate&lt;/a&gt;, enabling merchants to direct a fraction of their revenue to help scale emerging carbon removal technologies. In 2022 we launched &lt;a href=&quot;https://frontierclimate.com/&quot;&gt;Frontier&lt;/a&gt;, an advance market commitment to buy $1.8B+ of permanent carbon removal by 2040. In 2024, we entered our first multi-year offtake for clean energy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, Stripe’s corporate net zero program is entering a new phase. We are looking to streamline our emissions measurement, create a template for catalytic emission reductions, and champion buying removals on the path to net zero, all while meeting our expanding global ESG disclosure requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Stripe’s Climate Program Manager, you will set the strategy and lead the execution and reporting for Stripe’s corporate net zero program. You’ll partner with a wide range of stakeholders within and outside of Stripe – Accounting, Finance, Legal, Procurement, Facilities, Sales, and carbon accounting and assurance providers – to refine our greenhouse gas inventory, deliver a reduction and removal roadmap that meets our climate targets, and provide inputs to global ESG disclosures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires someone with expertise in carbon accounting and reductions strategy, sharp program and process management, a track record of getting big things done fast, and excellent judgement to make the ‘right’ recommendations for Stripe’s program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Net Zero strategy (~15%): &lt;/strong&gt;Own and evolve Stripe’s corporate net zero strategy, including Stripe’s transition plan, priorities, budget, annual goals, emissions forecasts, removal retirements, and progress tracking. Stay current on evolving disclosure requirements, net zero guidance, and industry best practices to ensure Stripe’s program is high impact and best in class&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Emissions measurement (~30%): &lt;/strong&gt;Build Stripe’s annual greenhouse gas inventory. Collect data inputs, evolve methodology, manage Stripe’s footprint vendors, run a rigorous and auditable process with cross-functional stakeholders, and identify opportunities to use AI to improve the process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Emissions reporting (~30%):&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Serve as Stripe’s subject-matter expert to deliver inputs to ESG controllership for regulatory disclosures and to customers for RFPs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reduction program (~25%):&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and manage emissions reduction initiatives across Stripe. This will include efforts like securing renewable electricity for Stripe’s scope 2 emissions, as well as supporting the creative and high-impact interventions like carbon removal or lower-emission data centers that we need to reach global net zero&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BA or BS degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-7+ years of experience in corporate sustainability, climate strategy, carbon accounting, environmental consulting, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent oral and written communication skills – especially adept at translating complexity into clear recommendations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of generating and implementing ambitious emissions reduction initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong quantitative skills and expertise in emissions accounting and Greenhouse Gas Protocol&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has led a corporate climate program in a sector with a significant Scope 3 footprint, ideally technology or financial services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is a self-starter, and has a proven track record of producing measurable reductions through clean energy, cloud usage, and other supplier engagement initiatives&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has a working knowledge of major emissions accounting and climate reporting standards and requirements (e.g., CSRD, California SB 253, GHG protocol), and experience with Watershed or similar enterprise carbon management&amp;nbsp; platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has experience partnering with cross functional controllership partners to manage a greenhouse gas inventory process that meets requirements for limited or reasonable assurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is an exceptionally fast learner. Enjoys (and has experience) quickly ramping on new reduction technologies and sustainability standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Global Business Services’ (GBS) Commercial Solutions team ensures operational and programmatic excellence across deal cycles, increases revenue through the development of transformative commercial constructs and/or operationalizing commercial readiness, and drives closure of Stripe’s sold portfolio. The team&#39;s reach is widespread across Stripe, not exclusive to one sales segment or geographical region; GBS drives change across go-to-market, positively impacting Stripe users, and cross-functional teams. GBS’s priorities are set through the direction of Stripe leadership and executive vision, partnership with sales and cross-functional organizations, as well as User feedback and market insights. This role sits within Global Business Practices’ Commercial Solutions team, responsible for developing, launching, and maintaining commercial constructs and operationalizing products for GBS readiness to drive revenue for Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Global Business Services’ Commercial Solutions team is looking for a Commercial Solutions Program Manager to own the end-to-end programmatic development of commercial and GBS launch readiness programs that drive revenue for Stripe. Programs have a large scope and/or impact in nature, including program managing first-of-its-kind commercialization efforts of acquired company product offerings, ongoing program support (pre to post-launch), custom deal support related to the program, ownership of related enablement and communications, as well as acting as a change agent across the business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be responsible for the end-to-end management of commercial and/or GBS launch readiness programs, driving cross-organizational alignment through the delivery of related outputs. This role requires a background in program management and commercial program experience, change management, a strong understanding of and experience in scaling global, cross-organizational mechanisms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The candidate will have experience in program ownership and management, custom pricing strategies, and a background in supporting selling motions. The candidate will have strong communication skills and executive presence to effectively communicate with Stripes from sellers, and Deal Strategies and Deal Pricing through to senior leadership. You will love this job if you are a natural relationship and mechanism builder.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently lead large scale, cross-functional commercial or GBS launch readiness programs that have Stripe-wide impact, often first-of-their-kind programs and initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and lead a highly complex program/s which require considerable resources and high levels of complex functional and technical integration and knowledge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the commercial program deal motion, partnering with Deal Pricing and/or Deal Strategy Strategists, sellers, and internal stakeholders to create custom commercial approaches&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally with sales teams, sales leaders, services/support teams, product teams, and cross-functional teams to develop, launch, and scale the commercial program (continuously evolving the ways Stripe goes to market) to support commercialization efforts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, surface, and action systemic, broad issues and gaps, proposing holistic solutions to address root causes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate, and propose creative solutions, through complex programmatic problems at scale across Go-To-Market and Stripe&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-functional teams such as Legal, Finance, Accounting, Service Teams, Product Teams, etc to resolve and remove internal blockers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as liaison within Sales, Deal Pricing and Deal Strategy Strategists, and other stakeholders for custom elements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate meetings, working sessions, and exercises that assist the leadership team in optimizing effectiveness amongst themselves and across the organization in general&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate on behalf of a position and quickly gain cross-functional alignment on the position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quickly build credibility and trust with internal stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead projects to solve existing commercialization issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BA/BS degree in Business, Technology, Finance, or Economics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in program management/commercial strategy/economics/deal management/pricing with experience owning program strategy or business operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of direct commercial pricing model program management skills/knowledge/experience/deal management, and/or oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving cross-team mechanism development end to end (ideation, planning, execution, launch, post-launch support)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in ambiguous, quickly scaling environments, comfortable with high-agency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging with senior executives on high priority initiatives, as well as the ability to work effectively across internal and external organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be able to articulate and understand business strategy at the C-Suite level to gain credibility and advise organizations on how best to achieve their business goals through the use of commercial programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication, presentation, negotiation, and project management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish credibility and maintain working relationships with internal stakeholders involved with commercial constructs (Legal, Finance, Accounting, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting data and metrics to senior leadership to report on metrics&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to advocate for a position even in the face of pushback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct commercial construct launch oversight and experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payments industry experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA degree in Business, Technology, Finance, or Economics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possess PgMP or PMP certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Terminal helps businesses extend their online presence into the physical world. Our mission is to make it as easy for businesses to accept in-person payments as Stripe has made it to accept payments online. We’re realizing the vision of unified commerce.&lt;br&gt;Terminal provides an integrated in-person payments platform spanning software, payment processing, device fleet management, and hardware. Our hardware portfolio includes Stripe-designed readers and accessories as well as devices from third-party hardware partners. Together, these products enable businesses to build reliable, differentiated in-person payment experiences across a broad range of use cases, countries, and operating environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Terminal TPM, you will become an expert on all things related to in-person payments. You’ll work with teams across Stripe to build, ship, and iterate on first-party as well as third-party hardware products in addition to advancing our work on Tap-to-Pay and beyond. You will partner closely with hardware engineering, firmware and software engineering, design, operations, logistics, partnerships, sales, finance, legal, and regional teams. Your work will require you to be in lock-step with Payments teams as well as card networks and Local Payment Method schemes, bringing unified commerce to life across our suite of devices. This is a highly cross-functional role for someone who can connect customer needs, technical constraints, business strategy, and execution across user experience, device capabilities, cost, quality, reliability, supply, and time to market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Independently define programs across Terminal including scoping, setting objectives, defining success criteria, and influencing resource allocation to deliver outcomes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Apply consistent prioritization and decision-making frameworks across your programs, driving high-velocity yet durable decisions that move the team forward without creating downstream debt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Identify obstacles and risks across Terminal’s cross-functional workstreams, proactively communicate them to stakeholders, and develop plans to address and prevent their recurrence&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Represent the voice of Terminal’s consumers and merchants to all stakeholders, translating user needs into clear program objectives and ensuring engineering and product decisions remain grounded in solving real problems&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Drive clarity across all stakeholders on goals, problems, and intended outcomes, serving as the connective tissue across Terminal sub-teams and their upstream and downstream dependencies. Operate similarly across Stripe, representing the Terminal org to collaborators in peer organizations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Develop a strong point of view on Terminal’s product development strategy and use it to define programs with measurable outcomes, adapting them as the product and user needs evolve&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Understand the technical challenges across Terminal’s systems, payment flows, identity infrastructure, fraud and risk models, money movement, and partner closely with engineering leads to define the most effective path to delivery&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of product management or technical program management experience, including managing programs across all phases of software development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of defining and executing complex programs across multiple functions in consumer-facing or payments products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to establish strong relationships with stakeholders and senior leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to navigate ambiguity, bring rapid clarity to multi-stakeholder problems, and drive teams toward effective solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of API design and high-level system architecture, sufficient to partner with engineering teams on program delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, commerce platforms, point-of-sale systems, or in-person payments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Card and Local Payment Method networks and schemes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a portfolio that includes both first-party products and third-party partner products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with sourcing, supply-chain risk, device pricing, unit economics, and global distribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payment-device certifications, local payment methods, accessibility requirements, connectivity, or regulated hardware environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience launching products internationally or a technical background in electrical engineering, computer science, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Growth team finds, engages, and onboards the engineers, finance professionals, scientists, and other domain specialists whose judgment teaches AI systems how to reason in their field. We&#39;re looking for a Growth Program Manager to own the programs that make that happen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is strategy and execution. You&#39;ll decide what to build and why, then build it. You&#39;ll take new initiatives from early and messy to scaled and repeatable, then move on to the next highest-impact problem. The programs you&#39;ll own are still being built, and you&#39;ll run them at a volume that surfaces problems nobody has seen yet. You&#39;ll use AI and automation to keep them from breaking as they scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for real ownership. You treat the program as your own, hold yourself accountable for the results, and don&#39;t wait for permission to fix what&#39;s broken.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the strategy for your programs: define goals, identify the biggest levers, and decide where to invest&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own execution end to end and be accountable for outcomes like pipeline, conversion, time-to-productive, and retention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead the teams that run your programs, including hiring leads who own their areas and setting clear expectations and performance standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build sustainable expert pipelines through targeted outreach, new channels, and creative approaches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build AI workflows and automations that replace manual work in sourcing, outreach, screening, onboarding, and reporting, such as LLM-drafted outreach, lead enrichment, triage agents, QA checks, and self-updating dashboards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand up reporting that shows how each program is performing, where the gaps are, and what to do about them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run a steady cadence of experiments on targeting, messaging, channels, process, and tooling, then turn what works into playbooks that people and agents can run&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with growth leads, operations, project teams, and vendors to align on priorities and keep work unblocked&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Once a program is in steady state, hand it off cleanly and take on the next one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in program operations, growth, recruiting or workforce operations, strategy and operations, or a similar role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve owned a program end to end, from setting the strategy to executing it. You were the person accountable when something broke, and the person who fixed it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You move comfortably between big-picture thinking and details, and you&#39;re as happy building a plan as you are working through a spreadsheet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and managing teams, ideally distributed or contractor-based&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment about prioritization when there&#39;s more work than time, and you know when to escalate and when to resolve on your own&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven: comfortable defining metrics, digging into funnels, and making decisions from imperfect data. You can run your own analysis in SQL or Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High agency and ownership. Ambiguity doesn&#39;t slow you down, and you thrive when given room to build something from nothing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve built things with AI. You use tools like Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, Claude Code, n8n, Zapier, Make, Retool, or Apps Script as a core part of how you work, and you have at least one workflow, automation, or tool you built that people actually used. We want to hear about what you&#39;ve built.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, concise writer and communicator. Much of this job happens over Slack and email, and clarity compounds across hundreds of interactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong candidates may also have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scaling a program through rapid growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A background in recruiting at scale, talent sourcing, growth marketing, or community building&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in marketplace, gig, or external workforce businesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Compensation packages at Scale for eligible roles include base salary, equity, and benefits. The range displayed on each job posting reflects the minimum and maximum target for new hire salaries for the position and may be inclusive of several career levels at Scale; it will be determined during the interview process based on work location and additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, qualifications, interview performance, and relevant education or training. Scale employees in eligible roles are also granted equity based compensation, subject to Board of Director approval. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for your preferred location during the hiring process, and confirm whether the hired role will be eligible for equity grant. You&#39;ll also receive benefits including, but not limited to: comprehensive health, dental and vision coverage, retirement benefits, a learning and development stipend, and generous PTO. Additionally, this role may be eligible for additional benefits such as a commuter stipend.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Please reference the job posting&#39;s subtitle for where this position will be located. For pay transparency purposes, the base salary range for this full-time position in the locations of San Francisco, New York, Seattle is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$180,800&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$226,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;PLEASE NOTE:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Our policy requires a 90-day waiting period before reconsidering candidates for the same role. This allows us to ensure a fair and thorough evaluation of all applicants.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Scale, our mission is to develop reliable AI systems for the world&#39;s most important decisions. Our products provide the high-quality data and full-stack technologies that power the world&#39;s leading models, and help enterprises and governments build, deploy, and oversee AI applications that deliver real impact. We work closely with industry leaders like Meta, &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ernst&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt; Young, Mayo Clinic, Time Inc., the Government of Qatar, and U.S. government agencies including the Army and Air Force. We are expanding our team to accelerate the development of AI applications.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We believe that everyone should be able to bring their whole selves to work, which is why we are proud to be an inclusive and equal opportunity workplace. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability status, gender identity or Veteran status.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with physical and mental disabilities. If you need assistance and/or a reasonable accommodation in the application or recruiting process due to a disability, please contact us at accommodations@scale.com. Please see the United States Department of Labor&#39;s &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12ScreenRdr.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Know Your Rights poster&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; for additional information.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We comply with the United States Department of Labor&#39;s &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Pay Transparency provision&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PLEASE NOTE: &lt;/strong&gt;We collect, retain and use personal data for our professional business purposes, including notifying you of job opportunities that may be of interest and sharing with our affiliates. We limit the personal data we collect to that which we believe is appropriate and necessary to manage applicants’ needs, provide our services, and comply with applicable laws. Any information we collect in connection with your application will be treated in accordance with our internal policies and programs designed to protect personal data. Please see our &lt;a href=&quot;https://scale.com/legal/privacy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;privacy policy&lt;/a&gt; for additional information.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Us&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Cloudflare, we are on a mission to help build a better Internet. Today the company runs one of the world’s largest networks that powers millions of websites and other Internet properties for customers ranging from individual bloggers to SMBs to Fortune 500 companies. Cloudflare protects and accelerates any Internet application online without adding hardware, installing software, or changing a line of code. Internet properties powered by Cloudflare all have web traffic routed through its intelligent global network, which gets smarter with every request. As a result, they see significant improvement in performance and a decrease in spam and other attacks. Cloudflare was named to Entrepreneur Magazine’s Top Company Cultures list and ranked among the World’s Most Innovative Companies by Fast Company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Cloudflare, we’re not looking for people who wait for a polished roadmap; we’re looking for the builders who see the cracks in the Internet that everyone else has simply learned to live with. We value candidates who have the instinct to spot a &quot;normalized&quot; problem and the AI-native curiosity to create a solution using the latest tools. Our culture is built on iteration, leveraging AI to ship faster today to make it better tomorrow, while ensuring that every improvement, no matter how small, is shared across the team to lift everyone up. If you’re the type of person who values curiosity over bureaucracy, and that AI is a partner in solving tough problems to keep the Internet moving forward, you’ll fit right in.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Available Locations: Austin, London, or San Francisco (Hybrid)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Search engines spent two decades learning what the web is worth: which pages are fresh, which sources are trusted, what people actually use. That knowledge came from watching how humans moved through the web.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Agents break that loop. AI models are trained and grounded on the web, but they have little visibility into what&#39;s changed, what&#39;s authoritative, or what&#39;s been fabricated. Site owners have it worse: AI crawlers already request content anywhere from a hundred to tens of thousands of times for every visitor they send back, and most have no idea how, or whether, they show up in AI answers. Both sides of the market are flying blind.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cloudflare sits in front of around 20% of the web and sees both sides of that exchange. Our team, the Agentic Internet team, is focused on making the web readable, discoverable, callable, and payable, built on open standards so no single company owns the rails. Signals &amp;amp; Data Products turns our network&#39;s view into products both sides can use: helping AI labs know what&#39;s fresh and trustworthy, and helping site owners see and shape how they show up in AI. Cloudflare believes in the open Internet, and we&#39;re in a position to help build the future where it thrives. Come help us make it happen! You can read more about some of our plans &lt;a href=&quot;https://blog.cloudflare.com/the-agentic-internet/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://blog.cloudflare.com/agentic-web/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the strategy for Signals, our web intelligence feed, and shape where our data products go next&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define what makes a signal worth paying for (freshness, provenance, trust, real-world usage) using data from Cloudflare&#39;s network&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build for both sides of the market: data products for AI labs, and visibility for site owners into how AI models find, use, and cite them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore what comes next, from knowledge graphs to measuring how sites show up in AI answers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver product specifications, prototypes, product positioning, and high-impact launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering, Data Science, Research, and GTM to ship at high velocity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Partnerships and BD on data partnerships with AI labs and other large buyers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the product externally with users, customers, AI labs, developers, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years as a technical PM, with experience shipping data, search, ranking, or ML products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep data fluency: you can reason about data quality, coverage, bias, and pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or selling data products or APIs (licensing, pricing, enterprise contracts) is a strong plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A builder: you get things done, can move quickly, and prefer &#39;show&#39; over &#39;tell&#39;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong communicator who is comfortable with ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team oriented: you&#39;d rather get it right than be right&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Cloudflare, performance is about outcomes (what you did) and behaviors (how you did it). We value curiosity, humility, empathy, and doing the principled thing. Learn more about our values on our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cloudflare.com/en-gb/careers/&quot;&gt;Careers page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be building a new product category from a vantage point no one else has, on a fast-moving team breaking new ground. You can read about our &lt;a href=&quot;https://blog.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-openai-discovery-agentic-web/&quot;&gt;early research here&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
